# bathos v0.6 Agentic Science Evolution — Sprint Composition

**Date:** 2026-05-26
**Task ID:** 260526_agentic-science-evolution
**Source spec:** `.praxia/docs/specs/260526_agentic-science-v06-evolution-spec.md` (oracle APPROVED pass 2)
**ADRs locked:** D2 manifest-hash-granularity · D3 adversarial-check-policy · D4 bypass-rate-split · D5 nonrepudiation-v06
**Status:** DRAFT — orchestrator to dispatch

---

## 1. Workflow Assignment Per Item

| # | Item | Template | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Exception-Swallowing Remediation | `bugfix_simple` | Mechanically enumerated sites; no new design surface; existing test suite sufficient to validate. `refactor_with_audit` would be overkill for targeted swallow replacements. |
| 2 | Pre-Execution Manifest | `spec_driven_dev` | Net-new `.bth.lock.toml` write path, schema v5 bump, and CLI command; needs test design for mtime-ordering verification. Too many decisions baked into atoms to treat as a bug fix. |
| 3 | `outcome="error"` First-Class | `bugfix_simple` | Single guard insertion at `runner.py:225`; atoms 3b–3d are downstream consumers of that guard. Regression risk is low and well-understood. No architectural ambiguity. |
| 4 | Structured MCP Error Taxonomy | `refactor_with_audit` | Replaces a freeform dict with a typed enum+dataclass; breaking change for any MCP client pattern-matching on the old payload; adversarial audit check ensures the version-2 payload serialization is correct. |
| 5 | Sprint-Audit Signals Extension | `spec_driven_dev` | Seven signals with entropy math, new DuckDB aggregates over `metadata` JSON column, and calibration thresholds — test design required upfront to avoid shipping uncalibrated signals without a harness. |
| 6 | `adversarial_check` Field + Lint + Enforcement | `spec_driven_dev` | New dataclass field, gate logic change in agent-mode, Tier-2 linter function with tautology deny-list; test design for asymmetric enforcement (D3) is non-trivial. |
| 7 | `bth cite <run_id>` | `bugfix_simple` | Net-new module but no architectural ambiguity; reads from warm DB via `query.get_run()`, formats output; atoms are independent and small. Recon + fixer + reviewer is the right shape. |
| 8 | `bth lineage --format prov` | `spec_driven_dev` | PROV-JSON mapping (6-concept table, `bth:` namespace, spec §4 Item 8) needs test design for backward-compat with `--format text` and single-run edge case. |
| 9 | PostToolUse NLM Hook (praxia) | `bugfix_simple` | Two atoms: shell script + JSON config patch; verification is a single live test. No design uncertainty. |
| 10 | Structured Gate Error Taxonomy (Rust) | `refactor_with_audit` | Rust enum mirroring Python enum; crate-placement ambiguity acknowledged in spec (praxia-core vs praxia-fsm); adversarial audit confirms serialization round-trip. |
| 11 | Locate Sprint-Composer (spike) | `bugfix_simple` | Pure research/locate spike producing a `.praxia/docs/research/` finding; one atom, no implementation; bugfix_simple maps correctly (recon → fixer-as-researcher → reviewer). |
| 12 | Loop Step Budget Enforcement (Rust) | `spec_driven_dev` | Four atoms spanning FSM state, config schema, loop-signature detection, and exhaustion handler; needs test design for the step-budget trigger before implementation. |

