## 2. Dependency DAG

**Explicit block relationships:**

- Item 3 blocks on Item 2 (atom-3b requires `outcome_error_reason` column from schema v5 declared in atom-2b)
- Item 6 blocks on Item 2 (atom-6d requires `adversarial_check_status` column from atom-2b; atom-6b requires `GateErrorCode.ADVERSARIAL_CHECK_MISSING` from Item 4, so Item 6 softly blocks on Item 4 — see cluster below)
- Item 4 blocks on Item 1 (atom-4b replaces `GateError(message)` introduced in atom-1b; the constructor overload must land on top of atom-1b's simple signature per spec evolution note)
- Item 5 blocks on Item 3 (`bypass_explicit` / `bypass_in_agent_mode` columns track `--no-sidecar` and `--agent-mode` fields from schema v5; `error_rate` signal requires `outcome="error"` to be populated correctly)
- Items 7 and 8 block on Item 2 (citation and lineage PROV require `manifest_sha256` and `manifest_path` fields from schema v5)
- Item 10 is independent of all bathos items (separate Rust crate); it logically precedes Item 12 (`praxia-fsm` step budget consumes `GateErrorCode` from Item 10)
- Item 12 blocks on Items 10 + 11 (step budget handler emits structured blocker using Item 10's enum; Phase 5 entry is conditional on atom-11a locate outcome)
- Item 9 and Item 11 have no blocking dependencies — they can ship at any time

**Dependency clusters:**

| Cluster | Items | Shared boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Schema foundation | 1 + 2 + 3 | Schema v5 (`schema.py`/`runner.py`); must land together |
| Error taxonomy | 4 + 6 | `prereg.py` / `GateErrorCode` enum; Item 6 gate check consumes Item 4 enum |
| Export cluster | 7 + 8 | Both read from warm DB post-v5; `cite.py` and `provenance.py` are net-new |
| Praxia Rust | 10 + 12 | Separate workspace; internal dependency only |
| No-dep items | 9 + 11 | Independent; can parallelize with anything |

**Cross-item file conflict — flagged risk:** Items 4 and 6 both modify `prereg.py`. Item 4 adds `GateErrorCode` enum and replaces `_gate_failure_payload`; Item 6 adds a gate check calling `GateErrorCode.ADVERSARIAL_CHECK_MISSING`. If dispatched concurrently they will conflict at `prereg.py`. Sequencing: Item 4 must merge before Item 6 work begins, or both must be dispatched in a single worktree with a combined fixer pass.

