## 5. Cross-Cutting Verification

**Schema v5 migration:**
- Responsibility: fixer in Batch 2 (`worktrees/v06-schema-foundation`)
- Test: run `bth migrate` against a copy of the current production catalog before merging Batch 2 PR; verify `manifest_sha256`, `manifest_path`, `outcome_error_reason`, `adversarial_check_status` all set to `""` on migrated rows
- Confirm `bth show <pre-v5-run-id>` displays "not recorded — pre-v0.6" for manifest fields (not empty string)

**Test files — new or extended:**
- Items 1–3: extend `tests/test_runner.py` and `tests/test_sidecar.py`; atom-1a specifically requires caller audit before test authorship
- Item 4: new `tests/test_gate_error_taxonomy.py` (MCP payload serialization round-trip)
- Item 5: new `tests/test_sprint_audit_signals.py` (entropy, unfired branches, overflow rate)
- Items 6: extend `tests/test_prereg.py` for agent-mode gate; new `tests/test_linter_adversarial.py`
- Items 7+8: new `tests/test_cite.py` · `tests/test_provenance.py`
- Items 10+12: Rust `#[cfg(test)]` inline tests in `gate_error.rs` and `praxia-fsm` step counter

**Manual smoke checklist (before declaring sprint complete):**
1. `bth run scripts/experiments/<any-stem>.py` — verify `.bth.lock.toml` exists before subprocess pid appears in `ps`
2. `bth run <script-that-exits-1>` — verify `bth show <id>` reports `outcome="error"` and `outcome_error_reason="exit_code=1"`
3. `bth run <agent-mode-script-missing-adversarial_check> --agent-mode` — verify `GateErrorCode.ADVERSARIAL_CHECK_MISSING` in MCP response
4. `bth sprint-audit` — verify 7-signal structured output including `bypass_explicit` and `bypass_in_agent_mode` as separate values
5. `bth cite <recent-run-id>` — verify manifest hash appears; `bth cite <pre-v5-run-id>` — verify "not recorded" fallback
6. `bth lineage <run-with-parent> --format prov` — verify `wasDerivedFrom` key in JSON
7. `bth lineage <run-with-parent> --format text` — verify backward compat unchanged
8. `bth lint` on sidecar with `adversarial_check` present — no warnings; on sidecar without — WARNING emitted

