## 6. Open Coordination Questions for Orchestrator

**Q1: Item 11 conditional re-promotion.** If atom-11a locates sprint-composer and it is well-bounded, should items 11b-11d (pre-registration gate node wiring) be folded into this sprint (Phase 5) or deferred to v0.6.1? **Recommendation:** defer to v0.6.1 even if found. Rationale: the locate spike (atom-11a) is ½ day; wiring a pre-registration gate node into an unfamiliar FSM component is L3 work not yet decomposed into atoms; cramming it into Phase 5 alongside Item 12 (loop budget) risks a rushed integration. Ship 12 clean; promote 11b-11d to v0.6.1 with a complete design sprint using the locate-spike output as its input.

**Q2: Item 5 `bth calibrate` helper.** Spec §4 Item 5 marks all thresholds as calibration targets; a `bth calibrate` command to set per-project baselines would let the researcher tune the signals against their own catalog. **Recommendation:** defer `bth calibrate` to v0.6.1. Shipping uncalibrated signals first is correct — you need to observe the noise floor before you can calibrate against it. Including calibration in this sprint adds scope before the signal behavior is understood.

**Q3: Praxia Rust work — separate worktree vs. bathos PR dependency.** Items 10 and 12 live entirely in the praxia repo; they have no hard dependency on bathos Python PRs. **Recommendation:** praxia work proceeds in its own worktrees and PRs on its own merge schedule, completely decoupled from bathos PR ordering. The only sequencing rule is: Item 12 (loop budget) dispatches after Item 10 merges in praxia. Bathos sprint is not blocked on praxia readiness.

**Q4: `linter.py` Tier-2 conflict risk (Items 4+6 combined worktree).** Both items modify `prereg.py` in incompatible ways if dispatched separately (Item 4 changes `GateError` signature; Item 6 adds a call using the new enum value). The combined-worktree approach in Batch 3a resolves this. Ensure the fixer prompt for Batch 3a explicitly describes atom-4b as a prerequisite within the worktree before atom-6b begins. This is not fully captured in the spec's per-item atom ordering — it crosses item boundaries.

**Q5: `schema.py` canonical serialization stability (D2 consequence).** ADR `260526_manifest-hash-granularity` notes that `sidecar.canonical_toml()` must be implementation-stable because any change breaks hash compatibility with prior manifests. There is currently no `canonical_toml()` method in `sidecar.py` (the method must be created in atom-2a). Before shipping Batch 2, the fixer should add a unit test asserting that `canonical_toml()` is deterministic across Python runs (key-ordering stability). This is a correctness invariant not explicitly called out in the spec atoms.

---

## 7. Sprint Exit Criteria

The sprint is complete when all of the following are observable:

1. **12 items merged to main** (or 11 items + item 11 explicitly deferred via `atom-11a` finding document)
2. **`uv run pytest` passes** with no skips on bathos integration tests
3. **`cargo nextest run` passes** on praxia crates affected by Items 10+12
4. **Schema v5 migration verified** on production catalog: `bth show` on a pre-v5 run ID displays graceful "not recorded" for manifest fields
5. **`bth sprint-audit` emits 7-signal report** including `bypass_explicit` and `bypass_in_agent_mode` as separate named values (D4 verified)
6. **`bth run <nonzero-exit-script>` produces `outcome="error"`** with `outcome_error_reason="exit_code=1"` — visible in `bth show`
7. **`bth run <agent-mode-script-no-adversarial-check> --agent-mode` is blocked** with `GateErrorCode.ADVERSARIAL_CHECK_MISSING` in MCP response
8. **`.bth.lock.toml` written before subprocess** — mtime check confirmed in smoke test
9. **`bth cite` and `bth lineage --format prov` produce valid output** with manifest_sha256 and PROV-JSON `entity`/`wasDerivedFrom` keys respectively
10. **PostToolUse NLM hook fires** and appends to `.praxia/nlm.jsonl` on any `mcp__notebooklm__*` tool call from a Claude Code session in praxia
11. **CHANGELOG.md updated** covering all 12 items (or 11+defer note)
12. **All four ADR files** (`260526_manifest-hash-granularity.md`, `260526_adversarial-check-policy.md`, `260526_bypass-rate-split.md`, `260526_nonrepudiation-v06.md`) present and linked from spec

